---
type: agent/instruction
Description: Review project changes
usage: "guide://_workflow/review"
aliases:
  - review
category: "project-workflow"
instruction: Perform a review of project changes in the current repository.
includes:
  - ../_partials/client-info
elicitation:
  review-target:
    message: Choose what to review in this repository.
    fallback: render
    schema:
      type: object
      properties:
        mode:
          type: string
          enum: [uncommitted, current-branch, branch, pull-request]
          description: Uncommitted work against HEAD, the current branch against the default branch, a named branch against the default branch, or a pull request in this repository.
      required: [mode]
  branch-name:
    message: Enter the branch to compare with the default branch.
    when:
      mode: branch
    fallback: render
    schema:
      type: object
      properties:
        branch:
          type: string
          pattern: '^(?!-)(?!.*\.\.)(?!.*//)(?!.*(?:^|/)\.)(?!.*[/.]$)(?!.*\.lock$)[A-Za-z0-9._/-]+$'
      required: [branch]
  pull-request-number:
    message: Enter the pull-request number in this repository.
    when:
      mode: pull-request
    fallback: render
    schema:
      type: object
      properties:
        pull_request_number:
          type: integer
          minimum: 1
      required: [pull_request_number]
---
{{h1}}Code Review

{{h2}}Review target

{{#kwargs.mode}}
{{#equals}}uncommitted{{kwargs.mode}}
Review the complete working tree against `HEAD`.
{{/equals}}
{{#equals}}current-branch{{kwargs.mode}}
Review the current branch against the repository default branch.
{{/equals}}
{{#equals}}branch{{kwargs.mode}}
{{#kwargs.branch}}
Review branch `{{kwargs.branch}}` against the repository default branch.
{{/kwargs.branch}}
{{^kwargs.branch}}
Ask for the branch name, then review that branch against the repository default branch. Do not start the review until the branch is named.
{{/kwargs.branch}}
{{/equals}}
{{#equals}}pull-request{{kwargs.mode}}
{{#kwargs.pull_request_number}}
Review pull request `#{{kwargs.pull_request_number}}` in this repository.
{{/kwargs.pull_request_number}}
{{^kwargs.pull_request_number}}
Ask for the pull-request number in this repository. Do not start the review until the number is given.
{{/kwargs.pull_request_number}}
{{/equals}}
{{#notequals}}uncommitted{{kwargs.mode}}
{{#notequals}}current-branch{{kwargs.mode}}
{{#notequals}}branch{{kwargs.mode}}
{{#notequals}}pull-request{{kwargs.mode}}
Ask the user to choose a supported review target before reviewing. Do not infer a target.
{{/notequals}}
{{/notequals}}
{{/notequals}}
{{/notequals}}
{{/kwargs.mode}}
{{^kwargs.mode}}
Ask the user to choose one target before reviewing. Do not infer a target.
- Uncommitted work compared with `HEAD`
- The current branch compared with the repository default branch
- A named branch compared with the default branch
- A pull request number in this repository
{{/kwargs.mode}}

{{h2}}General Guidance

- Evaluate changes against the agreed requirements and likely regressions.
- Check correctness, maintainability, security, and adequate behavioral coverage.
- Report concrete, actionable findings with their impact and recommended resolution.
- Do not modify production code or tests until the user confirms alignment on the required fixes.

{{#workflow}}
{{h2}}Guide Workflow Add-in

You MUST transition to REVIEW phase and read `{{workflow.file}}` to understand the current issue context.

{{#agent.class}}
{{#agent.has_handoff}}
  — If your current environment supports separate execution while preserving the ability to complete this review end-to-end, carry out this review workflow separately so it does not block the main interaction.
  — You may use a separate worker, subagent, delegate, or equivalent supported mechanism, but only if it can analyse the changes, produce or update the review artifact, and report the result successfully.
{{#agent.is_q_dev}}
  — If a subagent or delegate-style background execution mechanism is available here, prefer that mechanism before considering inline execution.
{{/agent.is_q_dev}}
  — If separate execution is not actually available here, say exactly: `Separate execution is not available here; continuing inline instead.`
{{/agent.has_handoff}}

{{b}}Review Instructions:{{b}}
  — You MUST NOT consider previous conversational history when conducting this review.
    {{b}}This review must be done with a fresh look without consideration of previous work, including any fixes and tests.{{b}}
  — Use {{#resource}}code-review{{/resource}} to access code review guidelines.
  — Read {{workflow.file}} to understand the current issue context {{#workflow.issue}}(issue: {{workflow.issue}}).{{/workflow.issue}}
  — Analyse the selected review target and create or update the review artifact in `{{#workflow.issue}}{{path.documents}}{{workflow.issue}}-review.md{{/workflow.issue}}{{^workflow.issue}}{{path.documents}}{{/workflow.issue}}`

{{#openspec}}{{b}}NOTE{{b}} Review artifacts are NEVER to be created in the openspec changes directory{{/openspec}}
{{/agent.class}}
{{^agent.class}}
{{>client-info}}
{{/agent.class}}
{{/workflow}}
